The browser's JavaScript engine is QuickJS-ng (https://github.com/quickjs-ng/quickjs), used under the MIT License:
  Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Fabrice Bellard
  Copyright (c) 2017-2024 Charlie Gordon
  Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Ben Noordhuis
Its source is vendored in crates/iyakki-js/vendor/quickjs-ng-0.17.0 together with its LICENSE file. It is compiled to
WebAssembly with the WASI SDK (LLVM, Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions), which links the WASI libc (wasi-libc: MIT and
Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions, with parts derived from musl, MIT) into crates/iyakki-js/assets/iyakki-js.wasm.


nanomp3 / nanomp3-core 0.2 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), a pure Rust port of minimp3 (CC0), decodes the MP3 radio streams.

The text is drawn with the DejaVu fonts (DejaVu Sans, Bold and Mono), which are free to use and redistribute under the
Bitstream Vera / DejaVu license; the license text is in crates/iyakki-shell/assets/DEJAVU-LICENSE.txt and travels with the fonts.
Hindi, Bengali, Gurmukhi, Gujarati, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Malayalam, Arabic and Hebrew text is drawn with Noto Sans fonts (Copyright Google Inc. / Google LLC), licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; the license text is in crates/iyakki-shell/assets/NOTO-OFL-LICENSE.txt. Text shaping uses rustybuzz (MIT) and unicode-bidi (MIT or Apache-2.0).

Radio stations offered as starting points were taken from the public Radio Browser directory (https://www.radio-browser.info);
the station names and streams belong to their broadcasters, and IYAKKI only links to the public streams.

Command-line tools installed from the CLI tile (kubectl, k3s, Helm, Terraform, GitHub CLI, AWS CLI, Google Cloud CLI, Azure CLI,
Arduino CLI, esptool, espflash) and the container images used for running code (python, node, alpine) are downloaded
from their vendors when a person asks for them. They are not part of IYAKKI and keep their own licenses.

Optional full web engine (only in the separate "web" image variant, never in the default images; see docs/FULL-BROWSER.md and
LICENSING.md item 9): WPE WebKit (LGPL-2.1+ / BSD-2-Clause), Cog (MIT), cage (MIT), wlroots (MIT), Mesa (MIT), GStreamer (LGPL-2.1+)
and the libraries around them are separate programs and dynamically linked shared libraries started by IYAKKI, not part of it. They keep their
own licences; the web image's legal-info/ directory carries their source and licence texts.
